    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: the anti-farming check on driver_profile has withheld the driver's payout (no_show_terminations_30d 5 against completed_trips_30d 40) — the escalation packet directs the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 in full."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute goes to a human reviewer. The SGD 4.50 cancellation fee is held — neither collected nor refunded — while the review is pending, and no money moves on this ruling.\n\nWhy the no-show itself is verified. The driver's record (EV-TRIP-03304) shows an 'I'm Here' event at 07:21:30, a free-wait timer starting at 07:21:32, and termination by the driver at 07:28:24 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, with no boarding event. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-03304, 100% coverage, 10-second cadence, no gaps) places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup geofence from 07:21:30 to 07:28:20 — a continuous in-geofence dwell of 410 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period carried in this trip's own platform_policy, the arrival marker matching the first qualifying fix to the second (offset 0.0 s, nearest approach 0.111 m). Limbs (a) to (d) of POL-NS-01 therefore all hold: the driver arrived, waited more than twice the required period, and cancelled 234 seconds after the dwell requirement was met at 07:24:30. The marker is genuine for POL-NS-05; there is no waiting-period shortfall for POL-NS-06 to refund; the wrong-entrance route of POL-NS-03 is not engaged because the stationary fixes were inside the arrival radius, not in the 50–400 m band; and POL-NS-10 has no waiting-time line to refund (waiting_time_fee 0.00). The chat (EV-CHAT-03304) confirms the rider was still on her way ('coming down now', 07:23:50). POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: limbs (a) and (b) are satisfied on the messages, but limb (c) affirmatively fails — the rider's own device sat 846–854 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius.\n\nWhy no payment can issue here. The payout that would otherwise follow under POL-NS-07 — 80% of the SGD 4.50 net fee, SGD 3.60 — is withheld by that clause's own anti-farming check on the driver's trailing-30-day figures: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 5 (4 or more) and 5 divided by completed_trips_30d of 40 is 0.125 (above 0.08). Both limbs are met, so compensation is withheld and POL-NS-09(d) makes escalation mandatory. Escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal: no monetary outcome issues and the SGD 4.50 is held. The escalation packet directs the reviewer to refund the rider's fee in full.\n\nOn the remaining points: the lifetime counter driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags (9) was not used — POL-GEN-01 makes it context only, and the anti-farming test reads the trailing-window counter, as the driver correctly put on the record. No artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08 (the arrived event matches the nearest GPS fix to the second; the trace has no gap; the chat sequence is intact and matches the record's message count of 2; the SGD 4.50 ledger line reconciles with platform_policy), so no discount attaches to the evidence and the confidence cap is 1.0. EV-ADVIS-03304-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT); it is not needed, because POL-NS-06 limb (i) accumulation is unnecessary where the single in-geofence interval already exceeds the minimum."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.50 cancellation fee in full — the clause's anti-farming check has withheld the driver's payout and routed the case to review, and POL-NS-09 holds the SGD 4.50 rather than collecting or refunding it meanwhile."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver — this dispute cannot be closed by an automated money ruling, and it goes to a human reviewer. Here is why, and what is still open.\n\nOn the trip itself the record is consistent and does support the no-show. The driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 07:21:30; the GPS trace places the car at the pickup pin from that same second and holds it there for a continuous 410 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period in force for this STANDARD pickup; and the driver cancelled at 07:28:24 under RIDER_NO_SHOW, 234 seconds after the required dwell elapsed. The rider's message 'coming down now' at 07:23:50, read at 07:24:20, and the rider's device sitting 846–854 m from the pin throughout the window confirm she had not reached the pickup. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 are met. POL-NS-05 finds the arrival marker genuine — the first qualifying in-geofence fix is at the marker's own second (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0) and the driver's nearest approach is 0.111 m, not more than 300 m away or moving — so no waiting clock is recomputed and no false-arrival referral arises. POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall (410 s against 180 s). POL-NS-03 is not engaged, because the stationary fixes are inside the 50 m arrival radius, not in the 50–400 m band. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider: limbs (a) and (b) are met (the driver neither replied within 120 s of her message nor placed an in-app call), but limb (c) affirmatively fails on the rider's own admissible fixes, so the dispute is decided under POL-NS-01.\n\nThe reason no money moves now is the driver's own profile. It records 5 no-show terminations in the last 30 days against 40 completed trips. That satisfies both limbs of the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check: 5 is at or above the count of 4, and 5 ÷ 40 = 0.125 is above the 0.08 rate. POL-NS-07 therefore withholds the driver's compensation — SGD 3.60, being 80% of the SGD 4.50 fee, the same figure the fare breakdown's money block computes — and requires escalation, which POL-NS-09(d) names as its own trigger. Under POL-GEN-03 escalation is terminal: no monetary outcome issues and the disputed SGD 4.50 is held rather than collected or refunded while the reviewer decides. The rider's claim that escalation is the only live route to her money is accepted; the driver's claim that POL-NS-07 fixes a SGD 3.60 payout is outweighed, by the anti-farming check operating on the very fields the clause names. The driver's own disclosure of that arithmetic is accepted as the correct reading of the correct fields. Any argument built on driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags (9) would be barred by POL-GEN-01 — a lifetime counter is context only and may not stand in for the trailing-30-day figure — but no kept claim relies on it, so nothing turns on it; it is recorded only as a context warning.\n\nThe open question for the reviewer, which belongs here rather than in the referrals: whether 5 no-show terminations in 30 days against 40 completions is fee-farming rather than a run of genuine no-shows. This single trip's no-show is independently verified on the trip record, the GPS trace and the chat log, so the reviewer should weigh the pattern and not re-try the arrival. The instruction POL-NS-07 attaches to an escalated packet is recorded in the referrals.\n\nEvidence and confidence: every artifact the findings rest on carries weight 1.0 — the trip record, the GPS trace, the chat log, the fare breakdown and both party profiles. The sole impaired artifact is the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-03304-01 at weight 0.0, which carries no fact and which no clause here relies on; it makes POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, and limb (i) is not needed because there is no dwell shortfall to accumulate across. Confidence 0.90, above the platform's 0.70 floor."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: the anti-farming check trips on driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d (5) against driver_profile.completed_trips_30d (40) — direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's SGD 4.50 cancellation fee in full; the fee is held rather than collected or refunded pending review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the driver and the rider: this case goes to a human reviewer, and the disputed SGD 4.50 is frozen — neither refunded to the rider nor paid out to the driver — while that review is pending. Here is why, on the figures in the record. The no-show itself checks out. The trip record shows the driver tapped 'I'm Here' at 07:21:30, and the GPS trace places him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius from that same second, with 42 consecutive qualifying fixes in one unbroken run (nearest approach 0.111 m) and a mean track position 2,323.9 m over the whole journey. He held position for 410 continuous seconds (07:21:30 to 07:28:20) against the 180-second free waiting period carried in this trip's platform_policy — an excess of 230 seconds — and cancelled at 07:28:24 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, 414 seconds after the waiting clock began. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold. The rider's case does not displace them: her own device sat 846.3 m to 854.2 m from the pin across all 74 fixes, outside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, so although she replied 'coming down now' at 07:23:50 and the driver posted no reply within 120 seconds (POL-NS-04 limbs (a) and (b)), limb (c) fails affirmatively and POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her, leaving the dispute on the driver's evidence under POL-NS-01. POL-NS-03 is not engaged (the driver's stationary fixes are inside the 50 m radius, not in the 50 m to 400 m band), POL-NS-05 finds the arrival marker genuine (first qualifying in-geofence fix at the marker second, dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0, so no false-arrival referral), and POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall (410 s against a 180 s minimum, single in-geofence run). What changes the outcome is POL-NS-07's anti-farming check on the driver's own trailing-30-day figures: 5 no-show terminations is 4 or more, and 5 divided by 40 completed trips is 0.125, above 0.08. Both limbs are met, so the driver's payout — 80% of the SGD 4.50 net fee, SGD 3.60, which the fare breakdown's own money block computes — is WITHHELD, and POL-NS-09(d) routes the case to human review. That is why no money moves now, and why POL-NS-07's direction to the reviewer (refund the rider in full) is recorded in the referrals. The rider's profile raises no counter-trigger: no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the 3 threshold, and the two parties have no prior no-show disputes against each other, so limb (c) is not met either. On evidence integrity: the trace is 100% covered at 10 s cadence with no gaps and both tracks present, the chat log's msg_id sequence is intact and matches the trip record's message count of 2, and the SGD 4.50 cancellation-fee line reconciles exactly with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50, so no artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08 and no discount applies. All artifacts used carry weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is not reduced. The presence of the rider's tracks and the driver's full arrival and dwell record is carried at weight 1.0 throughout. POL-GEN-01 excludes driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags (9, a lifetime counter) from any finding; only the trailing-30-day figures were read. Escalation is terminal, so the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold does not apply."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
